# mini-LMS decisions

Read `docs/DECISIONS.md`, `docs/CONTEXT.md`, and `docs/adr/` before changing scope.

- v1 is course pages: presentations, tests, and stored submissions. 3D chemistry labs, the pdb-viewer catalog, and offline `.labres` files are out of v1.
- Learners are adults. Names and email may be stored. Do not build the school pseudonym, PIN card, or teacher-key encryption scheme unless a later decision says so.
- A presentation is site pages. Do not ship the source PowerPoint or PDF to students and do not add a Download button. Do not claim screenshots are blocked.
- The teacher authors tests in a browser form: question text, a chosen number of options, LaTeX, basic formatting, and uploaded images. Hand-edited JSON is not the teacher's workflow.
- Published tests include which options are correct so the page can score on GitHub Pages. Do not mark the correct options for the student. After Check, show the score and which questions were right or wrong.
- A student types a name and no email for now. The stored name is whatever they typed. Do not add accounts or PIN cards for students in v1.
- v1 questions are choice questions only (one or many correct; text or image options) and are auto-scored. Numeric calculation items are post-v1.
- The teacher uploads a finished PowerPoint or PDF from a file dialog on the teacher pages. Students page through slides. Do not build a slide editor, do not offer the source file, and do not promise animations.
- Teacher pages (authoring, deck upload, submissions) require the teacher's name and password. The development login is stored only in the gitignored local file. Students have no password. A test or deck stays a draft until the teacher publishes it.
- Images in questions are uploads. Generate pictures in chat when asked, then the teacher inserts the file. Do not add an in-form image-generation button. A question may show one picture with its wording, and each option may have its own picture.
- Correct options stay unmarked on the test page. After Check, the student sees "Sent", the score, and which questions were right or wrong. Score in the browser from the published key so GitHub Pages can grade without a server. Retakes are a per-test switch, on by default. When the teacher server is running, each accepted submit is still a new attempt; the attempt number is per typed name + test.
- The teacher course list opens in sections: course, presentations, materials, each test, and each question. Method materials support bold, italic, links, alignment, and paragraphs.
- Score is all-or-nothing per question, one point each. Past attempts keep the test version that was submitted.
- A student on another computer opens the GitHub Pages site. Publish sends slide images into the repository so the site can show them. Do not commit the PowerPoint, PDF, or `data/` drafts. Do not promise that a visible slide cannot be saved.
- A submission is stored in full in Supabase, copied as a grade row to a Google Sheet, and announced in one Telegram line (time, course, test, name, email, score, attempt). Secrets for Sheets and Telegram stay off the public site. A Sheet or Telegram failure does not roll back a saved attempt.
